  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14186989/assets/635de7075b0d106ffc2a0f15e65ca7a3406a49945591aa5eae59090c74df1398.png)\n\nDue to the symmetry of the student's $t$-distribution, we have that $P(|X|\\ge x)=0.05$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\n2P(X\\ge x)=0.05\\,⟹\\,P(X\\ge x)=0.025.\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{T}_{11},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=11.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $10$ | $1.372$ | $1.812$ | $2.228$ | $2.764$ | $3.169$ |\n| $11$ | $1.363$ | $1.796$ | $2.201$ | $2.718$ | $3.106$ |\n| $12$ | $1.356$ | $1.782$ | $2.179$ | $2.681$ | $3.055$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 2.201)=0.025.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=2.201.$",
